				267,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Fix ExposeWorkbenchAccessor import markers and add service error isolation\n\nTwo fixes to the ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform that were causing SkyBridge bridges to silently fail:\n\n1. Import marker quote style: The transform was using single-quote import markers that matched stock VS Code source, but esbuild/Land's Output bundler rewrites quotes to double quotes in the post-bundle file. The marker mismatch caused `Source.includes(ImportMarker)` to return false, silently no-opping the entire `__CEL_SERVICES__` patch. All SkyBridge hooks (search registration, SCM, status bar, tree views) were offline because `__CEL_SERVICES__` stayed undefined.\n\n2. Service error isolation: Each `invokeFunction` is now wrapped in its own try-IIFE. Previously, a single failed service lookup (interface decorator missing in this profile, service not yet registered) would throw out of the entire `__CEL_SERVICES__` object literal, leaving the whole facade undefined. Now each service degrades to `null` individually, preserving all other bridges.\n\nRefs cf8dea549df816cc3b534beb9449f90bf678f69f (RewriteNodeModulesPath + expose IMarkerService)",
			"SHA": "f55a02821a2d7acad85060cf17796f62fda700d9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T01:03:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				267,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add RewritePerfBaselineWorker transform\n\nAdd a new build transform that fixes worker bootstrap crashes in the\nbundled editor's timer service. The transform replaces\n`timerService.js`'s `(function() { ... __name(fib, \"fib\"); ... }).toString()`\nperfBaseline worker source with a literal-string equivalent that omits\nthe cosmetic `__name(...)` decoration.\n\nSame OXC-mangling-truth fix as `RewriteNestedWorkerBootstrap`: when Vite\ninlines `timerService.js` into Sky's `_astro/partsSplash.*.js` chunk,\nthe chunk's `__name` helper gets mangled (e.g., `$4e`). The IIFE captured\nby `.toString()` carries the mangled `$4e` reference; the worker scope\nhas no `$4e` defined and crashes at module-eval with `ReferenceError:\nCan't find variable: $4e`. The literal-string replacement is\nmangler-immune.\n\nAlso update prepublishOnly.sh to gate debug profiles on `Debug=true`\ninstead of `NODE_ENV`. Tauri's `.env` file was silently overriding\nBuild.sh's `NODE_ENV=development` export, forcing `out-build` (mangled)\neven for debug builds that should pull from readable `out/`.\n\nRefs cf8dea549df816cc3b534beb9449f90bf678f69f (RewriteNestedWorkerBootstrap)",
			"SHA": "14cc0d5941bd561c41c6d5ffd190256cc92eafb9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T23:06:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				264,
				10
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add RewriteNodeModulesPath transform and expose IMarkerService\n\nAdd a new build transform and update an existing one:\n\n1. RewriteNodeModulesPath: Patch `vs/base/common/network.js`'s hardcoded paths (`vs/../../node_modules`, `vs/../../extensions`, etc.) to drop one `../` segment. Without this, the dev server resolves to `/Static/node_modules/` instead of `/Static/Application/node_modules/`, returns SPA `index.html` fallback, and all grammar/tokenization (textmate, oniguruma, language-detection) silently breaks across every extension.\n\n2. ExposeWorkbenchAccessor: Expose `IMarkerService` on `__CEL_SERVICES__.Markers` so SkyBridge can push extension diagnostics (rust-analyzer, TypeScript, ESLint) into the workbench. Mountain emits `sky://diagnostics/changed` events; the bridge now calls `Markers.changeOne(owner, uri, markers)` to paint red squiggles and populate the Problems panel.\n\nBoth transforms are idempotent and added to the BuildPipeline after RewriteNestedWorkerBootstrap.",
			"SHA": "cf8dea549df816cc3b534beb9449f90bf678f69f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T21:54:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				261,
				45
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Fix Monaco worker bootstrap crashes and add polyfill telemetry\n\nAdd two new build transforms that fix worker bootstrap crashes in the bundled editor:\n\n1. InjectWorkerBootstrapShim: Injects `__name`/`__defProp` shim into `webWorkerServiceImpl.js::getWorkerBootstrapUrl` blob factory so Monaco's language workers (TS/CSS/HTML/JSON services, semantic tokens) inherit the helpers in their module scope. Without this, workers crash with `ReferenceError: Can't find variable: $4e` when Vite/OXC mangling renames `__name` to `$4e`.\n\n2. RewriteNestedWorkerBootstrap: Replaces `polyfillNestedWorker.js`'s `(function... ).toString()` pattern with a literal JSON.stringified source that omits the cosmetic `__name(...)` decorations. The `.toString()` approach returns mangled source (`$4e`) which the blob worker can't evaluate since the identifier isn't defined in its scope.\n\n3. RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef: Replace hardcoded 2-file whitelist with auto-detection across all `vs/*.js` files - the whitelist silently failed because VS Code's out-build mangler emits different class names than expected.\n\n4. InstrumentVscodeGit: Add markers F (createModel done) and L (openRepository getRepositoryRoot done) for finer-grained Git extension activation diagnostics.\n\n5. Telemetry: Add global `__LAND_POLYFILL_TELEMETRY__` hook and wire it into ChildProcessPolyfill, IPCRendererShim, ProcessPolyfill, and SharedProcessProxy to route silently-caught failures to PostHog for monitoring.",
			"SHA": "e0fda068f1befeb3a76f470689b34bd8378fe554"
		}
	],
